1
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:01,400
Still so full of energy after working all night?

2
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:04,480
Wanna join?

3
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,360
I'm no good at this.

4
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,199
Come find me for badminton.

5
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:12,800
I can teach you.

6
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,599
It's late and quiet.

7
00:02:17,439 --> 00:02:19,599
It's better to just have a calm chat.

8
00:02:22,759 --> 00:02:24,000
We can chat in other ways, too.

9
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,400
You're not wearing yours?

10
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:40,719
I don't need to.

11
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:56,000
When did you find out about Lu Zhong?

12
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:56,680
That fast?

13
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,479
I found out later.

14
00:02:59,199 --> 00:02:59,879
How much later?

15
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,759
After I joined the Special Police Unit.

16
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,719
For that long,

17
00:03:03,719 --> 00:03:04,719
you kept it from us?

18
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,319
Confidentiality regulations.

19
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,479
I had no choice.

20
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:10,360
Then since you knew Jin Yonggang wasn't the killer,

21
00:03:10,599 --> 00:03:12,280
throwing a big celebration for the Third-Class Merit,

22
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,479
were you trying to mock us?

23
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:17,039
You...

24
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,039
I found out after the celebration.

25
00:03:19,039 --> 00:03:19,639
I don't believe you.

26
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,680
Then do you believe it wasn't just me

27
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,439
keeping it from you?

28
00:03:23,439 --> 00:03:25,120
Everyone kept it from the Special Police Unit.

29
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:35,439
Have you ever wondered

30
00:03:35,439 --> 00:03:37,039
why everyone kept it from the Special Police Unit?

31
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,319
Shouldn't you take a good hard look at yourself,

32
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:51,800
Liao Bufan?

33
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:17,800
Here.

34
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,120
What's this for?

35
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:22,040
We're out of ice. Put this on.

36
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,839
So it won't swell tomorrow.

37
00:04:54,439 --> 00:04:56,600
When I first joined the Special Police Unit,

38
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,160
I,

39
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,360
Liu Lang,

40
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:02,759
and Lu Zhong,

41
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,120
the three of us were the closest.

42
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,800
They were both older than me,

43
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,959
and always took care of me.

44
00:05:17,879 --> 00:05:19,360
Every time we went on a mission,

45
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,480
Lang would tell me,

46
00:05:22,959 --> 00:05:23,600
"Don't be afraid.

47
00:05:25,839 --> 00:05:27,000
Just stay behind me."

48
00:05:30,279 --> 00:05:31,839
Sometimes, to look out for me,

49
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:35,000
they'd take turns leading me when we split up,

50
00:05:36,079 --> 00:05:36,920
keeping me close.

51
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,279
When it was time for action, they went first.

52
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,480
That was in the past.

53
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,160
Special police forces nationwide had just formed.

54
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,480
It wasn't about whether conditions were good or not.

55
00:05:53,839 --> 00:05:56,199
Special police work on the edge of a knife.

56
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,000
It's different from you guys in the office.

57
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,759
Once, during an arrest operation,

58
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,480
we split up to search a compound.

59
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,120
When I rushed into a room,

60
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:13,360
a shot suddenly rang out.

61
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:15,959
I thought right then,

62
00:06:16,879 --> 00:06:17,279
"It's over.

63
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:19,879
I'm definitely going to die here."

64
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,040
That bullet

65
00:06:25,639 --> 00:06:27,199
grazed right past my head.

66
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,360
I lunged forward immediately.

67
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,319
He fired two more shots.

68
00:06:36,319 --> 00:06:36,680
Good thing

69
00:06:37,879 --> 00:06:38,560
he missed me.

70
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,399
That's when Lu Zhong arrived

71
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:45,360
and saved me.

72
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:48,680
Only later during the interrogation did I learn

73
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,560
that guy

74
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,920
had three murders on his hands.

75
00:06:56,079 --> 00:06:58,279
You and Lu Zhong have a life-and-death bond.

76
00:06:59,199 --> 00:06:59,639
I get it.

77
00:07:07,519 --> 00:07:09,199
Among us special police,

78
00:07:11,399 --> 00:07:12,439
we aren't just colleagues,

79
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,240
but rather

80
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,519
comrades who trust each other with our lives.

81
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,560
No matter where you come from,

82
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,560
or what your purpose is,

83
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:22,639
once you're here,

84
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,600
you have to leave all selfish thoughts behind.

85
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,120
This is loyalty.

86
00:07:29,879 --> 00:07:30,800
This is our mission.

87
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,480
Do you still think

88
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:42,600
that people like us

89
00:07:43,279 --> 00:07:44,120
are problematic?

90
00:07:50,399 --> 00:07:52,120
I'm saying all this just to tell you,

91
00:07:53,959 --> 00:07:55,199
this team of ours...

92
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:57,839
Loyalty,

93
00:07:58,439 --> 00:07:59,079
bravery,

94
00:08:00,639 --> 00:08:01,600
and dedication...

95
00:08:03,279 --> 00:08:03,800
None of that is a problem.

96
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,000
Valuing loyalty and emotions...

97
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,360
That's not a problem either.

98
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:10,560
The key is not letting them affect

99
00:08:11,439 --> 00:08:12,360
your judgment.

100
00:08:13,519 --> 00:08:15,000
Some sacrifices are inevitable.

101
00:08:15,439 --> 00:08:17,160
Some sacrifices are in vain.

102
00:08:20,279 --> 00:08:21,600
That's what being a cop is.

103
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,399
You successfully defused the bomb today,

104
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,079
but do you admit

105
00:08:28,079 --> 00:08:30,160
that you were distracted by Heihai?

106
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,639
Under those circumstances,

107
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,799
the chances of failure were too high.

108
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:40,600
If you had failed,

109
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,279
how would you face

110
00:08:43,279 --> 00:08:45,159
Liu Lang, who trusted you with his life?

111
00:08:46,879 --> 00:08:48,799
How would I explain it to his wife?

112
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:53,080
Say that Liu Lang trusted you till the end,

113
00:08:53,279 --> 00:08:54,320
with no regrets?

114
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:57,799
Wait, no.

115
00:08:59,039 --> 00:08:59,720
I'd be dead too,

116
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:00,759
so I wouldn't have the chance.

117
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:04,600
Someone else would have to hold a memorial for the three of us.

118
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,720
Then why did you still rush up there?

119
00:09:27,919 --> 00:09:28,480
We

120
00:09:29,639 --> 00:09:30,879
went through a bomb defusal.

121
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,519
Does that count as a life-and-death bond?

122
00:09:36,759 --> 00:09:37,799
You finally look like a real Special Police officer.

123
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:55,720
I'll cook you tomorrow.

124
00:09:56,639 --> 00:09:57,559
So I can nourish myself.

125
00:09:59,600 --> 00:09:59,840
Right.

126
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,759
When will you make some buns for us too?

127
00:10:04,559 --> 00:10:05,039
Seriously.

128
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,279
Sure.

129
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:10,879
Piece of cake.

130
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:13,039
What kind of filling do you want?

131
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:15,200
Anything's fine, as long as you make it.

132
00:11:22,639 --> 00:11:23,200
We

133
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,600
went through a bomb defusal.

134
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,320
Does that count as a life-and-death bond?

135
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,240
You're acting like a real Special Police officer now.

136
00:12:02,919 --> 00:12:03,679
Mom.

137
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:08,639
Did I wake you?

138
00:12:08,639 --> 00:12:09,600
Uncle Liao.

139
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,440
Is Mom back?

140
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,159
Your mom...

141
00:12:17,799 --> 00:12:19,159
Mom isn't back yet.

142
00:12:20,399 --> 00:12:21,399
Mom is sick.

143
00:12:21,799 --> 00:12:22,559
She's in the hospital.

144
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,279
What's wrong with her?

145
00:12:25,279 --> 00:12:27,279
Can I call Mom then?

146
00:12:27,679 --> 00:12:28,840
I miss her.

147
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
But the doctor said,

148
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,799
Mom can't use her phone right now.

149
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,799
If she uses her phone, she'll be just like you.

150
00:12:36,799 --> 00:12:39,039
She won't rest or sleep properly.

151
00:12:39,399 --> 00:12:40,919
So, once she gets better,

152
00:12:41,759 --> 00:12:42,799
she can use her phone again,

153
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,600
and then she can call you.

154
00:12:48,159 --> 00:12:49,799
It's okay. Mom will be better soon.

155
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:51,320
Really?

156
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:51,799
Really.

157
00:12:52,879 --> 00:12:53,559
Go back to sleep. Good.

158
00:13:07,919 --> 00:13:08,320
Okay.

159
00:13:09,399 --> 00:13:10,039
I got it.

160
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,240
Stay safe.

161
00:13:12,679 --> 00:13:13,279
Keep a close eye on them.

162
00:13:21,159 --> 00:13:21,639
Boss Lu.

163
00:13:22,559 --> 00:13:24,480
Da Yin has found their hideout.

164
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,639
It's where we used to cook.

165
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,919
Boss Lady must have taken them there.

166
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:36,360
Hidden in plain sight.

167
00:13:37,919 --> 00:13:38,320
Yeah.

168
00:13:39,279 --> 00:13:40,559
If we hadn't followed them all the way,

169
00:13:40,799 --> 00:13:42,000
who would've known they'd go there?

170
00:13:43,759 --> 00:13:44,240
Bro,

171
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:45,720
that place is very remote.

172
00:13:46,279 --> 00:13:46,960
Let's not wait.

173
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:48,200
Let's make our move tonight.

174
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,000
Let's wait for news first.

175
00:13:54,159 --> 00:13:55,639
Let's see how much information

176
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,759
the cops have gathered.

177
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,399
This place is very remote.

178
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:48,279
Few people around, and no internet.

179
00:14:49,399 --> 00:14:50,799
Security won't be an issue.

180
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:56,960
What is this place?

181
00:15:00,759 --> 00:15:02,480
The "Spring Snow" you got before

182
00:15:03,159 --> 00:15:04,320
was shipped from right here.

183
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,720
We can't stay at Lu Haifeng's place.

184
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:08,519
Then where else can we go?

185
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,799
This place has been abandoned for a long time.

186
00:15:19,679 --> 00:15:20,639
No one will come here.

187
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,840
There's something I've always wanted to ask you.

188
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,320
How did you know my identity?

189
00:16:16,919 --> 00:16:17,960
At a time like this,

190
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,440
is there any need to keep secrets?

191
00:16:42,159 --> 00:16:43,559
Someone sold your information

192
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,480
to Boss Bai.

193
00:16:50,919 --> 00:16:51,840
Boss Bai.

194
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,519
Only Lu Haifeng and his inner circle

195
00:17:02,519 --> 00:17:03,879
know my identity.

196
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:15,559
We managed to save his life.

197
00:17:16,039 --> 00:17:17,440
But due to excessive blood loss

198
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,480
and delayed treatment,

199
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,960
his brain tissue was damaged.

200
00:17:21,319 --> 00:17:22,400
I'm afraid he won't wake up anytime soon.

201
00:17:22,519 --> 00:17:22,880
Hold on.

202
00:17:23,039 --> 00:17:23,839
How long is "anytime soon"?

203
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,119
Can you give us an exact timeframe?

204
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:26,440
There's no exact timeframe for this.

205
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:27,759
Three to five days,

206
00:17:28,079 --> 00:17:28,599
a month...

207
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:29,440
Anything is possible.

208
00:17:29,759 --> 00:17:31,440
Alright, Doctor. Thank you.

209
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:32,319
You're welcome.

210
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:36,480
What do we do now?

211
00:17:39,599 --> 00:17:40,359
Looks like

212
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,480
we can't pin the progress of this case

213
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,960
solely on him.

214
00:17:46,839 --> 00:17:47,640
Those explosives,

215
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,440
we've already confirmed their source.

216
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:51,720
We'll investigate what we need to,

217
00:17:52,079 --> 00:17:53,039
and let him get the treatment he needs.

218
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:55,839
Right. Also,

219
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:58,359
announce to the public

220
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,000
that the suspect was shot and severely injured,

221
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,160
and has died from his injuries.

222
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:04,240
Got it, got it.

223
00:18:06,039 --> 00:18:06,440
Alright.

224
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,319
Let's split up.

225
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:09,640
You, keep an eye on him here.

226
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:10,160
Will do.

227
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:10,759
Let's go, let's go.

228
00:18:39,799 --> 00:18:40,400
Hold onto this.

229
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,000
Hello, comrade.

230
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:10,119
Police inspection.

231
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,200
Please show your ID.

232
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:22,599
What are all these people

233
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,480
heading out to do?

234
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,480
Night fishing.

235
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,160
They've been out at sea for two days.

236
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,960
Open this up. Let me take a look.

237
00:19:51,559 --> 00:19:52,200
No problem.

238
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:00,039
Open this one too.

239
00:20:19,839 --> 00:20:20,519
No problems here.

240
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:23,759
Everything's clear in the back, right?

241
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:24,519
All clear.

242
00:20:25,319 --> 00:20:25,799
Thanks for your cooperation.

243
00:20:26,039 --> 00:20:26,640
Thanks for your cooperation.

244
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:28,039
Good work.

245
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:36,359
Let's go take a look in the back.

246
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,039
That's what the bulletin said.

247
00:20:39,599 --> 00:20:40,640
Said he lost too much blood

248
00:20:40,839 --> 00:20:41,519
and couldn't be saved.

249
00:20:42,279 --> 00:20:43,400
It's good that he's dead.

250
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,680
Now everyone can rest easy.

251
00:20:47,359 --> 00:20:47,839
Boss Lu.

252
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,119
What do we do next?

253
00:20:53,559 --> 00:20:54,440
Let's find Pei Laosan.

254
00:20:55,559 --> 00:20:57,319
Make sure he doesn't fall into police hands.

255
00:20:58,880 --> 00:20:59,799
What about the Boss Lady?

256
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:07,759
Make preparations

257
00:21:09,519 --> 00:21:10,160
to bring her home.

258
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,079
The plane is taking off!

259
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,160
And landing!

260
00:21:28,559 --> 00:21:29,359
Take off!

261
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,559
Landing!

262
00:21:32,079 --> 00:21:32,839
Take off!

263
00:21:34,559 --> 00:21:35,440
Landing!

264
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:38,599
Chief Liao.

265
00:21:42,079 --> 00:21:42,599
Naonao, come down.

266
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:49,359
What's wrong, Brother Lang?

267
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,319
The CID guys

268
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:53,920
are checking the convenience store.

269
00:22:03,279 --> 00:22:03,759
Chief Na

270
00:22:04,359 --> 00:22:05,240
found some photos.

271
00:22:21,519 --> 00:22:21,880
Chief Liao.

272
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:22,960
Where's Chief Na?

273
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:23,680
He's inside.

274
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,160
Chief Na.

275
00:22:33,279 --> 00:22:34,720
I'm getting some toys for Naonao.

276
00:22:34,839 --> 00:22:35,680
And a change of clothes.

277
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:40,319
Is that okay?

278
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:41,440
Sure, take them.

279
00:22:46,319 --> 00:22:47,799
The kid's been with you guys these past few days, right?

280
00:22:48,519 --> 00:22:49,039
He's at the station.

281
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,839
Did he say anything to you guys?

282
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,319
Like what?

283
00:22:54,799 --> 00:22:55,720
He's a four-year-old.

284
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:56,799
Playing is all he thinks about.

285
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,039
He did.

286
00:23:00,599 --> 00:23:01,440
He said he wants his mom.

287
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:11,119
Have you found Yuan Lai?

288
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:14,559
I just don't get it.

289
00:23:15,559 --> 00:23:16,319
How did this foreign drug dealer...

290
00:23:16,319 --> 00:23:17,519
...manage to find this place?

291
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,160
I checked the security footage.

292
00:23:23,839 --> 00:23:25,200
Jester took Yuan Lai away.

293
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:28,680
Give it to me straight.

294
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,319
We're looking into it too.

295
00:23:36,319 --> 00:23:37,400
Did you find anything?

296
00:23:38,039 --> 00:23:38,559
Yeah, we did.

297
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:41,319
We found this.

298
00:23:46,079 --> 00:23:47,680
That's from when I took them to the amusement park.

299
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:48,359
Right, right.

300
00:23:49,119 --> 00:23:49,519
Chief Liao.

301
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,200
Listen, Zhang Peng and I...

302
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:53,319
...have been wanting to get tea and chat with you.

303
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:55,279
If you're free in a bit,

304
00:23:55,279 --> 00:23:56,319
let's head to the bureau together.

305
00:23:56,680 --> 00:23:57,799
Sure, sure. Sounds good.

306
00:23:58,400 --> 00:23:58,759
Let's go.

307
00:23:58,880 --> 00:23:59,920
Let's go right now, then.

308
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,240
What about the search?

309
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,680
Let Commissar Tan handle the search.

310
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:03,599
Alright.

311
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:04,519
Let's go, let's go.

312
00:24:19,039 --> 00:24:19,400
Commissar.

313
00:24:21,359 --> 00:24:22,759
Chief Liao told me to let you know...

314
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:25,200
...you're leading today's search.

315
00:24:26,799 --> 00:24:27,480
I'm leading it?

316
00:24:27,759 --> 00:24:28,279
Where is he?

317
00:24:30,119 --> 00:24:30,799
He went to the city bureau.

318
00:24:31,519 --> 00:24:32,279
The Task Force is looking for him.

319
00:24:33,599 --> 00:24:34,160
What for?

320
00:24:34,279 --> 00:24:34,759
I'm not sure.

321
00:24:38,640 --> 00:24:39,799
Na Haitao is coming over today.

322
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:40,920
Has he contacted you?

323
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:42,680
No.

324
00:24:44,119 --> 00:24:44,599
He's here.

325
00:24:45,039 --> 00:24:45,400
He is?

326
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,079
He's searching the convenience store by the gate.

327
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:48,759
Haoyunlai.

328
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,759
Searching the convenience store?

329
00:24:54,599 --> 00:24:56,039
I heard Old Na came by yesterday too...

330
00:24:57,119 --> 00:24:58,359
...and checked the security footage at the gate.

331
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:14,160
The kid's mother is missing.

332
00:25:16,079 --> 00:25:17,759
Chief Liao hopes you can

333
00:25:17,759 --> 00:25:19,440
submit a request to the higher-ups

334
00:25:21,039 --> 00:25:23,319
let the child stay with us for now.

335
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:28,680
At ease.

336
00:25:30,279 --> 00:25:30,759
Attention.

337
00:25:32,519 --> 00:25:33,480
Dress right.

338
00:25:37,519 --> 00:25:38,039
Eyes front.

339
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:42,599
Comrade Commissar.

340
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,519
Formation complete. Awaiting orders.

341
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:46,480
At ease.

342
00:25:48,359 --> 00:25:48,720
At ease.

343
00:25:51,119 --> 00:25:51,799
Comrades.

344
00:25:52,359 --> 00:25:54,240
You all know the suspect's basic details

345
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:55,119
clearly now, right?

346
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:56,400
Yes.

347
00:25:57,279 --> 00:25:57,960
Two requirements.

348
00:25:58,799 --> 00:25:59,440
First.

349
00:26:00,839 --> 00:26:01,279
Be thorough.

350
00:26:02,279 --> 00:26:02,960
Second.

351
00:26:03,839 --> 00:26:04,680
Stay safe, everyone.

352
00:26:05,319 --> 00:26:06,000
Yes, sir.

353
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:07,319
Good.

354
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,119
All personnel.

355
00:26:11,519 --> 00:26:12,000
Mount up.

356
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:13,480
Bai Jiani.

357
00:26:14,279 --> 00:26:14,519
Here.

358
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,599
You're not joining this operation.

359
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:18,880
You have a new assignment.

360
00:26:19,799 --> 00:26:20,079
Yes, sir.

361
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:21,799
Bomb disposal.

362
00:26:22,079 --> 00:26:22,400
Yes, sir.

363
00:26:23,599 --> 00:26:24,720
Commissar Tan went in personally

364
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,000
and defused the bomb with Chief Liao.

365
00:26:27,839 --> 00:26:29,759
Why meddle in a specialist's job?

366
00:26:30,599 --> 00:26:31,720
I don't know the details.

367
00:26:32,079 --> 00:26:33,039
I heard from the team

368
00:26:33,519 --> 00:26:34,640
he insisted on staying at the scene

369
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:36,240
and only left after the bomb was defused.

370
00:26:39,279 --> 00:26:40,200
No one was hurt, right?

371
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:40,960
No.

372
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:43,680
Did the operation go smoothly?

373
00:26:45,319 --> 00:26:45,880
We could've caught two,

374
00:26:46,519 --> 00:26:47,160
but one didn't show up.

375
00:26:49,599 --> 00:26:50,000
Chief.

376
00:26:50,759 --> 00:26:52,519
A city bureau assistance notice

377
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:53,759
asks us to organize personnel

378
00:26:53,799 --> 00:26:56,000
for a full search of our jurisdiction.

379
00:26:56,839 --> 00:26:57,119
This man,

380
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:58,319
Pei Jianguo,

381
00:26:58,519 --> 00:26:59,400
everyone calls him Pei Laosan.

382
00:26:59,519 --> 00:27:00,279
36 years old,

383
00:27:00,359 --> 00:27:01,799
a local fisherman,

384
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:04,000
suspected of organizing illegal entry.

385
00:27:04,799 --> 00:27:05,079
This one,

386
00:27:05,839 --> 00:27:06,599
Wu Sanlian,

387
00:27:07,079 --> 00:27:08,759
also known as Jester,

388
00:27:09,119 --> 00:27:10,599
is wanted overseas

389
00:27:10,599 --> 00:27:12,599
for drug trafficking and several murders.

390
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:13,880
Keep an eye on Jester.

391
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:14,880
He's extremely dangerous.

392
00:27:15,599 --> 00:27:16,279
And we now suspect

393
00:27:16,279 --> 00:27:17,519
he's connected to the Old Street case.

394
00:27:19,720 --> 00:27:20,720
Old Street?

395
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:21,880
Lu Zhong's case?

396
00:27:22,039 --> 00:27:22,400
Yes.

397
00:27:22,759 --> 00:27:23,279
Chief Ji.

398
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,880
I heard the suspect arrested yesterday

399
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,519
was the real killer of Commissar Lu.

400
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:29,680
The one who didn't show was an accomplice.

401
00:27:40,079 --> 00:27:41,119
Is Jin Yonggang really

402
00:27:41,119 --> 00:27:42,039
the one who murdered Lu Zhong?

403
00:27:44,079 --> 00:27:45,680
Based on the evidence we have so far,

404
00:27:46,119 --> 00:27:48,359
we still can't rule him out as a suspect.

405
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,640
But as for anything else,

406
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:52,559
we'll have to wait for further confirmation.

407
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:55,200
Then there's no need to hide this anymore.

408
00:27:55,519 --> 00:27:55,960
Wait.

409
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:58,240
The wanted poster is already out.

410
00:27:58,599 --> 00:28:00,440
This is out in the open now.

411
00:28:01,359 --> 00:28:01,960
What about Yuan Lai?

412
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:03,920
She must be involved in this case, right?

413
00:28:04,559 --> 00:28:05,559
She's definitely involved.

414
00:28:06,599 --> 00:28:08,079
Unfortunately, we were a step late and didn't catch her.

415
00:28:08,839 --> 00:28:09,480
You didn't catch her?

416
00:28:10,519 --> 00:28:11,279
Where did she go?

417
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:16,039
Ji Min, I...

418
00:28:16,759 --> 00:28:18,039
I've told you everything I can.

419
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:20,960
You're not on the Task Force,

420
00:28:21,799 --> 00:28:24,039
so I really can't tell you anything else.

421
00:28:24,599 --> 00:28:25,640
Alright, I understand.

422
00:28:47,359 --> 00:28:48,079
Come on.

423
00:28:48,079 --> 00:28:50,079
You used so much of my tea, isn't it bitter?

424
00:28:50,599 --> 00:28:52,000
Chief Liao is our guest here.

425
00:28:52,079 --> 00:28:52,960
Why are you being so stingy?

426
00:28:52,960 --> 00:28:53,680
I've noticed you're

427
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:55,400
a real cheapskate.

428
00:28:55,599 --> 00:28:56,359
You wouldn't part with a cent.

429
00:28:57,079 --> 00:28:57,400
Yeah.

430
00:28:57,480 --> 00:28:58,680
Chief Liao, try his good tea.

431
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:12,519
What exactly is going on with Yuan Lai?

432
00:29:18,599 --> 00:29:19,119
Well...

433
00:29:19,599 --> 00:29:21,000
The first time you met Yuan Lai

434
00:29:21,279 --> 00:29:23,480
was during that hostage situation, right?

435
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:24,039
Yes.

436
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:27,359
Was that the first time?

437
00:29:28,359 --> 00:29:29,119
Yes, it was.

438
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:30,680
No.

439
00:29:31,680 --> 00:29:32,720
Outside the mahjong parlor...

440
00:29:33,279 --> 00:29:33,920
you two had already met.

441
00:29:38,079 --> 00:29:38,640
I don't remember.

442
00:29:40,839 --> 00:29:42,000
You probably just didn't notice.

443
00:29:47,359 --> 00:29:48,160
Are you interrogating me?

444
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:57,839
And you're just sitting there

445
00:29:57,839 --> 00:29:58,559
chuckling away.

446
00:29:58,880 --> 00:29:59,599
I already told you.

447
00:29:59,599 --> 00:30:00,799
You call him all the way here,

448
00:30:00,839 --> 00:30:01,960
and fire questions at him like this.

449
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:03,559
How is this different from an interrogation?

450
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,960
You're really something, you know.

451
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:12,039
Chief Zhang, Chief Na,

452
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:13,799
my two good brothers.

453
00:30:14,839 --> 00:30:15,880
If you have questions, just ask directly.

454
00:30:19,599 --> 00:30:20,680
Alright, then I want to ask,

455
00:30:21,559 --> 00:30:22,400
about Yuan Lai.

456
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,000
Why did she open that shop

457
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:25,559
right outside your Special Police Unit?

458
00:30:26,599 --> 00:30:27,839
Well, when I was taking her home,

459
00:30:27,839 --> 00:30:30,079
she said she wanted to find a safe place.

460
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:33,039
The shop across the street was up for lease,

461
00:30:33,599 --> 00:30:34,319
so she took it over.

462
00:30:38,319 --> 00:30:39,039
You know all about this?

463
00:30:39,039 --> 00:30:40,200
You two must be pretty close, huh?

464
00:30:40,519 --> 00:30:42,200
Yeah, we are. We're neighbors.

465
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:45,119
Her kid is the one who's really close to him.

466
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:47,039
He's staying with Chief Liao right now.

467
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,839
Chief Liao just went to the store to grab clothes for him.

468
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:54,960
Naonao and I are indeed close.

469
00:30:56,319 --> 00:30:57,759
After the hostage situation,

470
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:02,079
he developed this gunshot stress disorder.

471
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:05,680
I took him to the bureau for counseling a few times.

472
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:07,559
Dr. Chen has all the records.

473
00:31:07,599 --> 00:31:08,359
You can check them.

474
00:31:09,880 --> 00:31:10,920
Dr. Chen also said

475
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:12,799
I should take him out to play when I can.

476
00:31:13,680 --> 00:31:14,480
He's a kid, after all.

477
00:31:14,759 --> 00:31:16,839
He gets close to whoever plays with him.

478
00:31:17,680 --> 00:31:18,599
Right, right.

479
00:31:22,319 --> 00:31:23,680
Then, in your eyes,

480
00:31:24,519 --> 00:31:25,640
what kind of person is Yuan Lai?

481
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:29,440
A good single mother.

482
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:30,680
No.

483
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:31,799
I mean,

484
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:34,920
have you, while spending time with her,

485
00:31:35,599 --> 00:31:36,440
noticed anything...

486
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,799
anything a bit off about her?

487
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:43,000
No.

488
00:31:48,599 --> 00:31:49,359
What do you think

489
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,160
is off about her?

490
00:32:06,519 --> 00:32:08,119
As for my relationship with Yuan Lai,

491
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:09,839
you can verify it yourselves.

492
00:32:10,279 --> 00:32:11,440
There's nothing to hide.

493
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:13,680
I don't know much about her past.

494
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:14,960
What I do know

495
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:17,839
is she's a single mom with a kid,

496
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:19,680
and across from our Special Police Unit,

497
00:32:19,680 --> 00:32:20,680
she opened a convenience store

498
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:22,160
to make a living.

499
00:32:22,559 --> 00:32:24,000
Do you know her social connections?

500
00:32:25,039 --> 00:32:25,799
She has an ex-husband.

501
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:27,720
Have you met him?

502
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,680
Yes. Lu Haifeng.

503
00:32:30,279 --> 00:32:31,240
The owner of Elite Club.

504
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:33,799
Yuan Lai told you that?

505
00:32:35,519 --> 00:32:35,920
What's wrong?

506
00:32:42,839 --> 00:32:44,279
Her file says she's unmarried.

507
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:55,240
Chief Liao, from what we've learned,

508
00:32:55,480 --> 00:32:57,519
Yuan Lai has no other real relatives.

509
00:32:58,319 --> 00:32:59,319
So about Naonao,

510
00:32:59,319 --> 00:33:00,960
should we apply

511
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:02,880
to find him a better care facility?

512
00:33:05,079 --> 00:33:06,200
Not for now.

513
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:08,319
Naonao's situation is special.

514
00:33:08,680 --> 00:33:10,119
He can't adjust to a new place.

515
00:33:11,279 --> 00:33:12,160
Until we find Yuan Lai,

516
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:13,440
he'll stay with me for now.

517
00:33:15,599 --> 00:33:16,079
We...

518
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:18,000
We just thought, you're a grown man,

519
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:18,839
looking after a kid...

520
00:33:19,359 --> 00:33:19,839
Well, this...

521
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:22,799
No offense, really. No offense.

522
00:33:23,079 --> 00:33:24,200
I don't mean anything else either.

523
00:33:25,400 --> 00:33:25,920
Don't worry.

524
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,039
Whatever I do,

525
00:33:28,400 --> 00:33:29,599
I've never betrayed this job.

526
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,279
If you need anything,

527
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:39,559
just tell us.

528
00:33:44,599 --> 00:33:45,160
You know, you...

529
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:46,359
Sometimes I hate to call you out.

530
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,119
Always saying you mean nothing by it.

531
00:33:48,279 --> 00:33:49,480
I'm telling you, it's over for you.

532
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:50,319
See?

533
00:33:50,839 --> 00:33:53,160
That nasty habit of yours is back.

534
00:33:56,279 --> 00:33:57,960
One, two, three.

535
00:33:59,359 --> 00:33:59,680
Go.

536
00:34:07,839 --> 00:34:08,400
Once more.

537
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:10,400
Come on.

538
00:34:11,199 --> 00:34:12,679
Three, two, one.

539
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:23,800
Your Uncle Liao is here.

540
00:34:24,119 --> 00:34:25,079
Uncle Liao.

541
00:34:26,039 --> 00:34:26,360
Go on.

542
00:34:27,679 --> 00:34:28,360
He's playing.

543
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:29,000
Chief Liao.

544
00:34:29,599 --> 00:34:30,440
Why didn't you go check leads?

545
00:34:31,599 --> 00:34:33,000
Commissar Tan gave me a new task.

546
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:34,039
He told me to play with Naonao.

547
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:38,159
Playing with him wore you out?

548
00:34:39,159 --> 00:34:40,760
It's tougher than a five-k run.

549
00:34:41,519 --> 00:34:42,400
Then get some rest.

550
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:43,239
You get the day off today.

551
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:44,960
Don't you need my help?

552
00:34:45,039 --> 00:34:45,440
No.

553
00:34:45,719 --> 00:34:45,960
Take it.

554
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:46,679
Let's go.

555
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:57,039
Big Goose.

556
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:07,039
Uncle Liao.

557
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:09,679
Big Goose is protecting Naonao.

558
00:35:09,880 --> 00:35:11,400
Naonao won't fear nightmares now.

559
00:35:11,800 --> 00:35:13,440
I just made a deal with it.

560
00:35:13,719 --> 00:35:15,679
It promised to protect Uncle Liao too.

561
00:35:17,559 --> 00:35:18,239
That's great.

562
00:35:19,159 --> 00:35:20,639
From now on, Uncle Liao and you

563
00:35:21,199 --> 00:35:22,239
are in Big Goose's care.

564
00:35:25,199 --> 00:35:27,000
But what about Mom?

565
00:35:28,079 --> 00:35:29,960
Big Goose isn't by her side.

566
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:32,000
Who's going to protect her?

567
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:45,440
Then let's buy a big goose for Mom too.

568
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:47,920
Wouldn't that protect her?

569
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:49,800
Right?

570
00:35:52,760 --> 00:35:54,800
Then can you help me hang these clothes up?

571
00:35:55,239 --> 00:35:56,199
These are all your clothes.

572
00:35:59,159 --> 00:36:00,039
Can you do it? Look.

573
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:02,920
Just hang them.

574
00:36:11,480 --> 00:36:12,079
Who wants to start?

575
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:18,360
Well, it's like this.

576
